WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.300
People drive on the left and distances are in miles (mph). A licence from a European Economic Area country (such as Spain): you can usually drive while it is valid.

2
00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:29.300
A licence from other countries (for example Colombia or Venezuela): you can drive for 12 months from when you become resident here; after that you must exchange it, if your country is on the list, or pass the British test.

3
00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:45.300
Always check with the official GOV.UK tool, because it depends on the country and the type of licence. To use a car you need insurance, vehicle tax and, if it is over 3 years old, an MOT test.

4
00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:52.900
London has zones with a daily charge (ULEZ, Congestion Charge): check before you drive in.

5
00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:58.500
Say it aloud: “Can I drive with my licence?”.
